  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1226 AM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nAnother shortwave drops southeast out of the central Rockies into \nthe Southern Plains on Thursday. This wave could provide another \nquick shot of rainfall across portions of central and northern \nOklahoma. A few storms appear possible, but no severe weather is \nanticipated. \n\nTemperatures through the latter part of the week and into the \nweekend should remain rather consistent in the upper 60s and \nlow/middle 70s. Models do show another large upper low dropping \nsouth through the northern Plains and into the mid-Mississippi River \nValley over the weekend, but any precip associated with this wave \ncurrently appears to remain to our north and east. It will also \nbring another front through the area Saturday and Saturday night.",
